t to the+AAoA-extent that warranties are provided), that licensees may convey the+AAoA-work under this License, and how to view a copy of this License.  If+AAoA-the interface presents a list of user commands or options, such as a+AAoA-menu, a prominent item in the list meets this criterion.+AAoACgAA  1. Source Code.+AAoACgAA  The +ACIA-source code+ACIA for a work means the preferred form of the work+AAoA-for making modifications to it.  +ACIA-Object code+ACIA means any non-source+AAoA-form of a work.+AAoACgAA  A +ACIA-Standard Interface+ACIA means an interface that either is an official+AAoA-standard defined by a recognized standards body, or, in the case of+AAoA-interfaces specified for a particular programming language, one that+AAoA-is widely used among developers working in that language.+AAoACgAA  The +ACIA-System Libraries+ACIA of an executable work include anything, other+AAoA-than the work as a whole, that (a) is included in the normal form of+AAoA-packaging a Major Component, but which is not part of that Major+AAoA-Component, and (b) serves only to enable use of the work with that+AAoA-Major Component, or to implement a Standard Interface for which an+AAoA-implementation is available to the public in source code form.  A+AAoAIgAA-Major Component+ACIA, in this context, means a major essential component+AAoA(kernel, window system, and so on) of the specific operating system+AAoA(if any) on which the executable work runs, or a compiler used to+AAoA-produce the work, or an object code interpreter used to run it.+AAoACgAA  The +ACIA-Corresponding Source+ACIA for a work in object code form means all+AAoA-the source code needed to generate, install, and (for an executable+AAoA-work) run the object code and to modify the work, including scripts to+AAoA-control those activities.  However, it does not include the work's+AAoA-System Libraries, or general-purpose tools or generally available free+AAoA-programs which are used unmodified in performing those activities but+AAoA-which are not part of the work.  For example, Corresponding Source+AAoA-includes interface definition files associated with source files for+AAoA-the work, and the source code for shared libraries and dynamically+AAoA-linked subprograms that the work is specifically designed to require,+AAoA-such as by intimate data communication or control flow between those+AAoA-subprograms and other parts of the work.+AAoACgAA  The Corresponding Source need not include anything that users+AAoA-can regenerate automatically from other parts of the Corresponding+AAoA-Source.+AAoACgAA  The Corresponding Source for a work in source code form is that+AAoA-same work.+AAoACgAA  2. Basic Permissions.+AAoACgAA  All rights granted under this License are granted for the term of+AAoA-copyright on the Program, and are irrevocable provided the stated+AAoA-conditions are met.  This License explicitly affirms your unlimited+AAoA-permission to run the unmodified Program.  The output from running a+AAoA-covered work is covered by this License only if the output, given its+AAoA-content, constitutes a covered work.  This License acknowledges your+AAoA-rights of fair use or other equivalent, as provided by copyright law.+AAoACgAA  You may make, run and propagate covered works that you do not+AAoA-convey, without conditions so long as your license otherwise remains+AAoA-in force.  You may convey covered works to others for the sole purpose+AAoA-of having them make modifications exclusively for you, or provide you+AAoA-with facilities for running those works, provided that you comply with+AAoA-the terms of this License in conveying all material for which you do+AAoA-not control copyright.  Those thus making or running the covered works+AAoA-for you must do so exclusively on your behalf, under your direction+AAoA-and control, on terms that prohibit them from making any copies of+AAoA-your copyrighted material outside their relationship with you.+AAoACgAA  Conveying under any other circumstances i